          "id": 1187010959,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> While here use wmem_strbuf_get_str() instead of wmem_strbuf_finalize().\n> \n> Accepted best practice is to let the scope free the memory. Removing the finalize call avoids an unnecessary realloc.\n\nI always interpreted wmem_strbuf_finalize as the wmem equivalent of g_string_free. Would it make sense to get rid of the realloc? If not, we might want to at least add something like \"you probably want to use wmem_strbuf_get_str instead\" to the wmem_strbuf_finalize documentation.",
